SAMPLE [heading] The function
SAMPLE   {f(x) = (sin(x))^(2)*cos(2*x)}
SAMPLE on the interval −π/4 ≤ x ≤ π/4.
SAMPLE [heading] Step 1 · Domain
SAMPLE f is defined for every x.
SAMPLE On −π/4 ≤ x ≤ π/4 it is defined and continuous, so there are no vertical asymptotes here (and on a closed interval no horizontal ones either).
