SAMPLE   A product is 0 exactly when one of its factors is 0:
SAMPLE   • sin²x = 0
SAMPLE     sin x = 0
SAMPLE       ⇒ x = πn
SAMPLE       Inside the interval (n = …, −1, 0, 1, …):  x = 0
SAMPLE   • cos 2x = 0
SAMPLE     cos(2x) = 0
SAMPLE       ⇒ 2x = π/2 + πn
SAMPLE       None of these lie inside the interval.
SAMPLE   [result] On −π/4 < x < π/4:  x = 0
