SAMPLE [subheading] The derivative
SAMPLE   Differentiate and factor:  {f′(x) = ((2*(x)^(2) - 3))/(x)}
SAMPLE [subheading] Solve f′(x) = 0
SAMPLE   A fraction is 0 when its numerator is 0. The denominator x is positive (ln x needs x > 0), so solve 2x² − 3 = 0:
SAMPLE   2x² − 3 = 0:  Δ = b² − 4ac = 0² − 4·2·(−3) = 24
SAMPLE     x = (−b ± √Δ)/(2a) = (0 ± √24)/4  ⇒  x = √6/2 (≈ 1.22)  or  x = −√6/2 (≈ −1.22)
