SAMPLE   −∞ < x < −2:   f″(−6) ≈ −0.281 < 0   ∩ bends down
SAMPLE   −2 < x < ∞:   f″(2) ≈ 0.281 > 0   ∪ bends up
SAMPLE [subheading] Conclusion
SAMPLE   [result] No inflection points: the bending only changes across an asymptote, which isn't part of the graph.
